.. raw:: html

      <div class="sphx-glr-thumbnail-title">Harmonic vs. Morse IR band positions, and recovering anharmonicity from overtones</div>
    </div>


.. only:: not html

 * :doc:`/api/gallery/spectro/vibrational/plot_01_harmonic_vs_morse`

.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Raman and Krishnan (1928) found that a small fraction of scattered light is shifted in frequency by a molecule&#x27;s vibrational wavenumbers. A mode is Raman-active if it changes the molecule&#x27;s polarizability. It is infrared-active if it changes the dipole moment. For a centrosymmetric molecule such as CO2, no mode is active in both spectra.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/spectro/vibrational/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_03_raman_ir_mutual_exclusion_thumb.png
